{"kind":"request","text":"Research note: agentic development practice and the journey (notes/2026-10-26-agentic-development-practice-survey.md).\n\nHugh asked on 26 October 2026 whether the processes planned for the journey (plan 032, section 2b) are flexible enough for development practice that is changing quickly. The note reads Linear's next-system page, the Capy documentation and the Claude Code team's \"How the Claude Code team does code review\" (read at its claude.dev mirror; the X post is behind a payment wall), plus a merge-queue analysis, two arXiv papers and practitioner writing. It states seven things the sources have in common, compares each practice with what dap records at main a97c7425 and with the landing policy, evidence rules, hosted agent teams and roles notes, and asks for each practice whether a room can adopt it by publishing data or needs a platform version.\n\nSection 6 records Hugh's five decisions of 26 October 2026: (1) the rules say who lands, the exit test's rules require a person, and H2 is replaced by the landing policy's two routes; (2) a finding item joins the change lane with a merge guard on open findings from a required source; (3) the agent wake over an authorized event feed is part of J5 and lands before the exit test; (4) the membership version that makes roles data (trusted authors, reviewer agents recorded apart from approval) is filed now as a design request; (5) the exit test measures human approvals per change, wait on a person and reverts, with one tier-0 extent. Section 7 proposes the order for plan 032's next draft: the finding item at J3's position, J5 with the wake, the exit-test rules before the exit test; the destination version (two routes, combined with the evidence-rules version), the membership version and parallel reservations after measuring.\n\nDocuments only. The note commissions nothing. The planner's next head amends plan 032 (draft 3) from it.","body":{"conditions":"One planner head adding notes/2026-10-26-agentic-development-practice-survey.md: documents only; every path:line citation resolves at main a97c7425 to the fact stated; quoted external sentences are quotations with their source in section 8; dap described, not ranked; decisions stated as Hugh's and commissioning nothing; prose lines at most 79 characters; check-doc-links 0 broken; check-notes 0 warnings; one checker review at the exact head before landing; no deployment.","target_head":"a97c7425f860273ee0c37f9a4f3631bf2b24bfed","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}